| .control
| save all
| * Each point is a COLD-START, SETTLED transient, not a bare
| * unconstrained .op (issue #172, contract #171): `uic` starts every node
| * at its natural cold value with EN low (the testbench's VEN steps high
| * at 101us), so the block powers up through its own soft-start ramp and
| * no operating-point solve happens at all. v(vout) is averaged over the
| * settled 199ms-200ms tail. 200ms is this bench's own measured
| * requirement, not a round number: at the ratified row's 0mA endpoint the
| * feedback divider is the only discharge path out of the 1uF C_OUT, so
| * v(vout) at tt/27C/3.30V reads 1.85985V over 0.8ms-1ms and only reaches
| * its settled 1.80239V after ~100ms. A 1ms window there reports a 57mV
| * load regulation that is pure unsettled-transient artifact. The 50mA
| * endpoint settles inside 1ms at every corner probed. See the testbench
| * header for the full settling measurement.
| * --- point 1: I_LOAD = 0 (no load, deck default) ---
| tran 10u 200m uic
| meas tran vout_0ma avg v(vout) from=199m to=200m
| * --- point 2: I_LOAD = 50mA (altered, full load) ---
| alter iload = 50m
| tran 10u 200m uic
| meas tran vout_50ma avg v(vout) from=199m to=200m
| let meas_load_reg_v = abs(tran2.vout_50ma - tran1.vout_0ma)
| let meas_load_reg_pct = 100*abs(tran2.vout_50ma - tran1.vout_0ma)/1.8
| print meas_load_reg_v
| print meas_load_reg_pct
| quit
| .endc
| .end

